Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||05-25-2000||07:47 PM||||it looks like i have a buyer for my 86SE- the only problem is he cannot tow it over the grapevine here in CA, and the only car i have to tow with is my 87GT. is there anyone around who would maybe help out with the towing in exchange for some money, gas, etc? i really need this car gone, and it seems like he wants it, i just cant tow it there. thanks in advance for any replies! BTW- if you think of something i could do for you in exchange for it, ask and i will see what i can do.||||reg||1
Z||000001||phillip||05-26-2000||09:50 AM||||tow it over the grape vine? i don't understand that so this may not help you at all. i just rented a u-haul truck with a tow dolly to tow a fiero about 150-170 mls. $80 deposit (refunded) about $220 for actual rental that incuded not quite 300 mls. in the deal (one way rental). figure in gas and dep. refund and it cost me about $180. i also had to catch a greyhound up to where the car was, but you may not have that problem. an idea anyway.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroSTETZ||05-26-2000||11:47 AM||||well, the problem is that I am getting about 500 for the car, so spending almost 300 to get it there is too expensive.||||reg||1
Z||000003||phillip||05-26-2000||12:25 PM||||if you can get something to tow with the dolly itself is about $40. the best i can offer suggestion wise.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||05-27-2000||01:10 PM||||The Grapevine is a really big hill/mountain in California.  On I-5 if I remember correctly.  It's a b**** in a big truck with a light load.  I can't imagine a Fiero pulling another Fiero over it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||V6pack||05-27-2000||01:41 PM||||This is Stetz's prospective buyer.  My Ranger V6 won't pull that hill without overheating, and God knows what else, and Shawn's G-Pa's 4 banger PU won't do it either.<P>I talked the Shawn ths morning and we agreed on this:  I will pay $50. and the fuel up from Oceanside to the base of the hill on the Bakersfield side....and Shawn will pay $50. and fuel for the return to Oceanside.  So... $100. and fuel to someone with a PU and some time to kill.<P>That is about all we can do to make it work.  Transport of a "dead" car from Stetzville to me is $400!!!  So, we are out of options.<P>Thanks for the space..any interested can contact Stetz for the best day/time, since I'm free anytime. <P>v6pack||||reg||1
